Port the code-generator scripts to Lua 5.2 and later.

tolua++ is mostly written in Lua: src/bin/lua/*.lua parse the .pkg file and
emit the binding.  They are 5.0-era code and use plenty of what 5.1 and 5.2
took away.  Grouped by cause:

* table.getn / table.foreach / table.foreachi (gone in 5.2) -> # and
  pairs/ipairs.  compat.lua's own shims for these were themselves written in
  terms of the removed functions.
* math.log10 / math.mod / math.frexp / math.ldexp (gone unless Lua is built
  with LUA_COMPAT_MATHLIB, which MSYS2's is not) -> math.log(x, 10),
  math.fmod, and dropped for the two with no replacement and no caller.
* loadstring, unpack, setfenv (gone in 5.2) -> load, table.unpack, and
  load()'s fourth argument.
* string.gfind (renamed in 5.1) -> string.gmatch.
* The implicit vararg table `arg` and its `n` field (gone in 5.1) -> {...}
  and select('#', ...).  compat-5.1.lua faked `arg` by rewriting the text of
  every script it loaded, substituting "...)" for "...) local arg = ...;".
  That substitution is blind -- it fires inside call expressions too, so
  `return string.format(...)` became a syntax error the moment the scripts
  stopped being loadable any other way -- and it never applied to the copies
  embedded in toluabind.c, which are what a released binary actually runs.
  Retired along with the last caller.
* "\." and "\[" inside patterns.  Lua 5.1's lexer let an unknown escape
  stand for the character itself; 5.2 made it an error.  Both are respelled
  the way Lua always read them.

Upstream: not submitted (project unmaintained since 2012); the AUR
          tolua++_5.3 package carries a subset of these
Applies-to: all environments
